# User-Level Instructions

Identity: ${USER_NAME} <${USER_EMAIL}>.

## Git

- Commit, push, or open PRs only when asked.
- Conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `chore:`, `perf:`, `style:`, `build:`, `ci:`, `revert:`); enforced by the global git commit-msg hook (`git-hooks/commit-msg`). No emojis.
- No AI attribution anywhere: no `Co-Authored-By`, no "Generated with", no AI comments. `settings.json` sets `attribution` to empty strings.
- No workflow jargon in commit or PR text (`wip:`, `stream A`, `review-vN`, finding counts); write what a human developer would.
- Never stage paths in `${CLAUDE_HOME}/config/never-stage.txt` (`.env*`, `credentials*`, keys, `docs/` workflow files); `hooks/bash-guard.py` enforces it.
- Claude-specific ignores go in `.git/info/exclude`, never `.gitignore`.
- No direct pushes to `main`/`master` (`git-hooks/pre-push` and `hooks/bash-guard.py`); branch first.

## Directories

- `docs/` — local AI workflow notes (plans, progress, reviews). Never committed.
- `documentation/` — real project docs. Committed. Render with the `docs-writer` skill.

## Base branch detection

```bash
BASE=$(git symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD 2>/dev/null | sed 's@^refs/remotes/origin/@@')
[ -z "$BASE" ] && BASE=$(git branch -l main master 2>/dev/null | head -1 | awk '{print $NF}')
[ -z "$BASE" ] && BASE="main"
git rev-parse --verify "$BASE" 2>/dev/null || echo "ERROR: Base branch '$BASE' not found locally."
```

## Working style

- Verify before claiming done: run the build/tests after each change.
- Prefer serena (symbol navigation) for finding definitions/references and symbol edits in code repos; Grep/Glob for text, config and docs.

## GitHub (when the repo has a GitHub remote)

Use `gh` and keep work traceable on GitHub:
- Non-trivial task: find a matching issue (`gh issue list --search`) or create one with labels before starting. Split multi-part work into sub-issues (`gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{n}/sub_issues -F sub_issue_id=<id>`, where `<id>` is the child's database id from `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/<num> -q .id`, not its number).
- Branch `<type>/<issue#>-<slug>`. PR via `gh pr create` with `Closes #N`, matching labels and milestone; open as draft until checks pass (`gh pr checks --watch`).
- CI failure: read it with `gh run view <id> --log-failed` before guessing.
- Bugs or follow-ups found outside the task's scope: open an issue instead of fixing silently or dropping them.
- Workflows and parallel agents: one issue or sub-issue per stream; post one short progress comment per milestone and link each PR to its issue.
- Releases: tag, then `gh release create` with notes from the merged PRs.
- Ask first before closing, transferring or deleting issues, changing repo settings, or commenting on other people's issues/PRs.

